# viola-config: Design

TOML configuration parser for `viola.toml`. `#![no_std]`, no alloc. Parses the lint-host config that a viola consumer authors to declare gates, severity rules, and per-issue pattern overrides.

The TOML surface is documented in `docs/VIOLA-TOML-V2-SCHEMA.md`; this document summarises the parsed in-memory shape.

## Config root

### `ViolaConfig`

The parsed top-level config. Carries gate thresholds, lint config blocks, and severity rule overrides. The crate's primary value type; every consumer call site receives one of these.

### `parse`

Entry point for the parser. Takes input bytes and returns `Result<ViolaConfig, ConfigError>`. Zero-copy slicing into the input; the resulting `ViolaConfig` borrows from the input via lifetimes the caller manages.

### `parse_default`

Convenience wrapper around `parse` that fills in default values where the input is silent. Used by callers that want to materialise a `ViolaConfig` even when the consumer has not supplied an explicit `viola.toml`.

### `ConfigError`

Enum of the parser's error variants. Each variant names the kind of malformedness encountered (unknown key, type mismatch, schema violation, etc.).

## Gate config

### `GateThresholds`

Numeric thresholds for the compound and file-count gates. Applied to the diagnostic batch after a run to decide whether the run succeeded or failed by gate.

### `GateOverride`

Per-issue override carrier that shadows the default thresholds for a specific issue pattern. Used when a consumer wants to relax or tighten a gate for one category without changing the global defaults.

### `SEVERITY_FILES_CAP`

Default cap for the files-affected gate. Applied when no override matches the diagnostic.

### `SEVERITY_COMPOUND_CAP`

Default cap for the compound-condition gate.

### `SEVERITY_PARTIAL_FILES_CAP`

Default cap for the partial-severity files-affected gate (a narrower scoping than the full cap).

## Lint config

### `LintConfigBlock`

Per-lint config payload that gets passed to the lint cdylib as the `lint_config_bytes` arg in `LintEvaluateVtable.evaluate`. The block's contents are opaque to viola-core; only the target lint interprets them.

## Severity rules

### `SeverityRule`

Full-severity rule. Carries an issue-pattern match plus an impact override. Applied to diagnostics post-evaluation to adjust their effective severity.

### `PartialSeverityRule`

Partial-severity rule for narrower scoping. Lets a consumer adjust severity for a subset of an issue category without rewriting the full rule.

### `CompoundOp`

Enum naming the compound-condition operators. Variants: `And`, `Or`. Used inside `IssuePattern` for boolean composition.

## Issue patterns

### `IssuePattern`

Parsed issue-match pattern. Used by severity rules to select which issues a rule applies to. Carries category match, impact match, and optional compound conditions composed via `CompoundOp`.

### `parse_issue_pattern`

Parser entry point for one pattern string. Returns `Result<IssuePattern, IssuePatternError>`.

### `IssuePatternError`

Enum of the issue-pattern parser's error variants.

### `Category`

Enum naming the high-level issue categories (correctness, style, performance, etc.).

### `Impact`

Enum naming the impact levels (low, medium, high, etc.) used as severity overrides in rules.

## Design notes

`#![no_std]` with no alloc to match viola-cli's `#![no_main]` constraint. Parser uses zero-copy slicing into the input bytes; `ViolaConfig` borrows from the input bytes through lifetimes the caller manages. No internal allocation; all storage is the caller's buffer.

## Slice 2a additions

The owned-form bridge that lets `viola_config` data slot into a `hilavitkutin_api::Resource<T: 'static>`. The borrowed `ViolaConfig<'a, N>` stays for parser output; the owned shape below is what every WorkUnit reading the parsed config consumes.

### `ViolaConfigOwned`

Owned-form viola config. Generic over five const parameters: `MAX_PLUGINS`, `MAX_GATES`, `MAX_RULES`, `MAX_PARTIAL_RULES`, `ARENA_BYTES`. Carries fixed-cap arrays for plugins, gates, rules, and partial rules each paired with an `arvo::Cap` length tracker, plus a private `arena: ConfigArena<ARENA_BYTES>` field that backs every `Str` handle interned during parse. The bundle is `'static` (no borrows escape) and slots into `Resource<T>` directly.

### `ViolaCfg`

Workspace-default alias for `ViolaConfigOwned`. Instantiates with the workspace cap parameters: `MAX_PLUGINS`, `MAX_GATES`, `MAX_RULES`, `MAX_PARTIAL_RULES`, `ARENA_BYTES`. Consumers reference this alias rather than the full generic instantiation.

### `ConfigArena`

Crate-private fixed-cap byte arena. Implements `hilavitkutin_str::ArenaInterner`. Slice 2a ships the type with `unimplemented!()` `arena_intern` and `arena_resolve` bodies; Slice 2b wires the real intern path. The constructor is `#[doc(hidden)]` so Slice 2a callers do not accidentally trigger the trap.

### `ConfigBytes`

Raw bytes of the workspace `viola.toml`, populated by the host shim at scheduler-builder time. `LoadConfig` reads this Resource and parses into `Resource<ViolaCfg>`. Fixed-cap byte array plus `arvo::Cap` length tracker; `CONFIG_MAX_BYTES = 16384` caps the buffer at 16KB.

### `CONFIG_MAX_BYTES`

Maximum byte length of the raw `ConfigBytes` buffer the host shim hands to `LoadConfig`. Workspace-default `16384` (16KB). Pre-1.0; observed real viola.toml configs stay well under 4KB.

### `MAX_PLUGINS`

Maximum number of plugins in one `ViolaConfigOwned`. Workspace-default `16`. Honours the existing `ViolaConfig<'a, const MAX_PLUGINS: usize>` default. Pre-1.0; observed real configs use 2 to 4 plugins.

### `MAX_GATES`

Maximum number of `[gates]` entries in one `ViolaConfigOwned`. Workspace-default `32`. One gate per lint; pre-1.0.

### `MAX_RULES`

Maximum number of `[[severity]]` rules in one `ViolaConfigOwned`. Workspace-default `64`. Per-lint severity overrides; pre-1.0.

### `MAX_PARTIAL_RULES`

Maximum number of `[[severity.partial]]` rules in one `ViolaConfigOwned`. Workspace-default `16`. Per-lint partial-match severity overrides; pre-1.0.

### `ARENA_BYTES`

Arena byte capacity for one `ViolaConfigOwned`. Workspace-default `8192` (8KB). Backs every `Str` handle interned during parse. Pre-1.0; sized for typical plugin-name plus rule-string totals with 2x headroom past observed configs.

The existing `ViolaConfig` section above remains the source-of-truth for the borrowed-form parser output. `ViolaConfigOwned` is the bridge for the `Resource` boundary; the two coexist.
